NiriFX compositor development package
===================================

This recipe builds the complete NiriFX patch stack from the NiriFX main branch
and its exact upstream Niri revision. It is a development candidate, not a
published or physically accepted compositor release. It is paired with the
niri-fx-git tools package; rebuild both when testing a new source revision.

The package installs a candidate at /usr/lib/niri-fx/session-candidate and the
separate "NiriFX (package)" login entry. Stock Niri supplies niri.service,
niri-session, shutdown handling and portal configuration. Its executable,
login entry and service files remain unchanged. No package hook adopts a
candidate, changes a user's configuration, or starts a session.

Adopt explicitly as your normal user, after reviewing your existing Niri config:

  /usr/bin/niri-fx native adopt --candidate /usr/lib/niri-fx/session-candidate \
    --config ~/.config/niri/config.kdl

Review the proposed files and plan_sha256. Repeat the command with --apply and
--expect-plan REVIEWED_SHA256 only when you want to retain that candidate and
select it for the next login. Adoption copies the compositor, configuration and
tools into private retained storage. A package upgrade does not switch that
selection. For later adoptions, omit --config to preserve the current settings:

  /usr/bin/niri-fx native adopt --candidate /usr/lib/niri-fx/session-candidate

Review that new plan before repeating it with --apply and --expect-plan.
Unsupported existing managed installations are preserved and refused
with migration guidance, rather than silently replaced.

After successful adoption, log out and select "NiriFX (package)". An unprepared
user receives an actionable error; login never adopts or selects a candidate.
Keep the ordinary "Niri" entry available for recovery. The packaged entry has a
different filename from previously registered per-user niri-fx.desktop entries.
Do not use pacman --overwrite or delete another user's entry to resolve a clash.

Install xdg-desktop-portal-gnome for screencasting and xdg-desktop-portal-gtk as
the fallback portal. The stock niri-portals.conf may use GNOME's file chooser,
which requires Nautilus unless a user explicitly selects GTK for FileChooser.
X11 applications need xwayland-satellite. Shell, notification, secret-service
and authentication-agent choices remain yours; this package does not add shell
service dependencies or alter portal settings.

Removing this package removes its candidate, dispatcher and chooser entry.
It leaves retained per-user bundles and configuration alone. Use stock Niri or
reinstall the package to regain its chooser entry. Retained native binaries still
depend on system libraries; retaining them does not freeze a distribution ABI.

Validation boundaries
---------------------

Builds use the full ordered patch stack, release/default desktop features and
locked dependencies. Cargo fetching occurs in prepare(); compilation and native
regressions run offline. makepkg's later stripping/debug processing is disabled
because the producer records the final executable after stripping it itself.
The exported provenance uses relative paths, and the final installed hash must
match its manifest.

The disposable-container acceptance harness checks payload ownership, two-user
adoption, stock-file preservation, package removal and retained selection.
Running that harness is a separate gate after building the candidate; this draft
recipe does not imply a passing result. Those checks do not establish
display-manager login, portals/PipeWire, lock/unlock,
suspend/resume, physical input, mixed monitors, graphics resets or GPU behavior.
Known native capture limitations remain applicable. Require the project's native
acceptance gates before publishing a supported full-session package.

From a disposable official Arch container with the checkout mounted read-only,
run the harness as root with explicit archives built from the reviewed source:

  NIRIFX_ARCH_PACKAGE_CONTAINER=1 bash scripts/test-arch-session-package.sh \
    /output/fresh-run /packages/niri-fx-git.pkg.tar.zst \
    /packages/niri-fx-compositor-git.pkg.tar.zst

An optional second tools/compositor archive pair checks that package replacement
leaves both users' selections unchanged. It does not apply the replacement
candidate or prove a version upgrade. The harness refuses host execution and
records which optional checks ran. It installs dependencies inside the container;
it neither builds packages nor fetches project source.
